  "body": {
    "focus": "Both codex paths of CliProvider (structured completion src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:274-278 and review session :386-390) send codex the strict form of the caller's schema, produced by the existing processSchemaForOpenAIStrict (src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts:266) on a copy, so the caller's schema object is unchanged. A test shows a schema without additionalProperties reaches codex's --output-schema file in strict form in both paths and the caller's schema is not modified. Implements ISSUE-e48e33ae6af03720.",
    "producesLld": false,
    "commit": "f141774d",
    "tasks": [
      {
        "id": "s1",
        "passed": false
      }
    ],
    "summary": "This Story's own change is dd771653 only: both codex paths of CliProvider write codexSchemaJson(schema) = processSchemaForOpenAIStrict(structuredClone(schema)) to --output-schema; test src/agent/providers/__tests__/cli-codex-strict-schema.test.ts (fake codex records the schema file; three falsifying mutations each fail it). Its recorded range (from ca2c1c2e) also contains three later, separately tracked bugfixes that I sequenced after it before this gate passed: ISSUE-ae2d83c6 (687395c8, judge prompts), ISSUE-91640def (08c023de, dcc39996, trivial gate test pick), each with its own ISSUE, gate, code review and approved BUILD, plus their record commits and two --no-ff merges of upstream docs. Those are not this Story's scope. Live: with the daemon on dd771653+, codex accepted the judge schema (no HTTP 400) and every gate since has run on codex.",
